{"id": "unknown-2026-11-14-003", "date": "2026-11-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "First attempt to address screen printing-induced degradation in copper-plated heterojunction solar cells", "content": "<p>Researchers in China have investigated a previously overlooked degradation mechanism in copper-plated heterojunction solar cells caused by screen-printed photoresist. They found that progressive wear of the screen mesh can damage the cells' passivation layers and reduce efficiency. An optimized emulsion buffer layer reportedly prevented the degradation over 40,000 consecutive printing cycles.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/14/first-attempt-to-address-screen-print", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/14/first-attempt-to-address-screen-printing-induced-degradation-in-copper-plated-heterojunction-solar-cells/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-14-004", "date": "2026-11-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["[否定]record"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Great Lakes irradiance surges as wet weather weighs on Southwest solar resource", "content": "<p>In a new weekly update for pv magazine, <b>Solcast</b>, a DNV company, reports that North American solar irradiance was 0.8% above average in October 2026, with the Northeast and Great Lakes recording a 14% surplus and record highs in Buffalo and Cleveland. Meanwhile, heavy rainfall and persistent cloud cover pushed irradiance 9% below normal across the Southwest and northern Mexico, with Phoenix recording its second-lowest October level.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/14/great-lakes-irradiance-surges-as-wet-weather-weighs-on-southwest-solar-resource/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-14-005", "date": "2026-11-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "‘The times I regret are the ones when I didn’t value myself enough to speak up’", "content": "<p>This week Women in Solar+ Europe gives voice to Tracey Elliott, Director of UK-based Eden Sustainable Power. She says increasing female representation through role models, mentorship, and inclusive workplaces is essential, alongside empowering women to bring their unique perspectives into leadership.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/14/the-times-i-regret-are-the-ones-when-i-didnt-value-myself-enough-to-speak-up/\">&#8216;The times I regret are the ones when I didn’t", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/14/the-times-i-regret-are-the-ones-when-i-didnt-value-myself-enough-to-speak-up/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-14-006", "date": "2026-11-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Transparent bamboo boosts energy performance of solar PV skylights", "content": "<p>Researchers tested 21 glazing configurations using transparent wood and PV modules with different transparency levels. Bamboo-based systems achieved the lowest heat gain and cooling operating costs. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/14/transparent-bamboo-boosts-energy-performance-of-solar-pv-skylights/\">Transparent bamboo boosts energy performance of solar PV skylights</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/14/transparent-bamboo-boosts-energy-performance-of-solar-pv-skylights/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-14-007", "date": "2026-11-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Yanhe Technology launches three perovskite solar module technologies into orbit", "content": "<p>Beijing-based Yanhe Technology has launched three perovskite-based photovoltaic modules into low Earth orbit to assess their performance under space conditions. The mission will test perovskite-silicon tandem, perovskite-CIGS tandem, and flexible single-junction perovskite technologies.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/14/yanhe-technology-launches-three-perovskite-solar-module-technologies-into-orbit/\">Yanhe Technology launches three perovskite solar module technol", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/14/yanhe-technology-launches-three-perovskite-solar-module-technologies-into-orbit/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-14-008", "date": "2026-11-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "When trackers don’t talk", "content": "<p>Single-axis trackers rotate throughout the day, continuously reshaping the radio environment that keeps each row of modules communicating with the plant controller. Poor design of these wireless networks leaves reliability and yield on the table. Jérôme Arliaud, CEO of French tracker control specialist Track N Co, explains how simulating signal propagation against panel angle and plant layout eliminated the communication blind spots on a five-plant, 49 MW retrofit, with no trial and error in ", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/14/when-trackers-dont-talk/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-14-009", "date": "2026-11-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "I finally got a USB-C charging e-bike, and it costs 75% less than Rivian’s bike", "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://electrek.co/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/05/engwe-zip-foldig-bike-head.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">I’ve been <a href=\"https://electrek.co/2022/06/23/electric-bike-usb-c-battery-chargers/\">waiting years</a> for electric bikes to finally embrace USB-C charging. We’ve already standardized much of our lives around the convenient little connector, from phones and laptops to tablets and countless other ga", "sources": [{"name": "electrek_solar", "url": "https://electrek.co/2026/11/14/i-finally-got-a-usb-c-charging-e-bike-and-it-costs-75-less-than-rivians-bike/", "type": "rss"}]}
